comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-10T09:11:30.892Z",codex,"Duplicate check: fresh all-status schema, tracker root, and membership searches plus open/in-progress lists found the completed implementation pmc-3jq8 and unrelated historical owners, but no owner for these two new PR #188 compatibility findings. Reuse pmc-3jq8 lineage through this review-fix child. Sources: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/pull/188#discussion_r3977389940 and https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/pull/188#discussion_r3977412690"
  "2026-09-10T09:18:45.259Z",codex,"TDD evidence: the new real Git fixtures first failed with an empty root pathspec and rejection of a historical custom status by current schema rules. Physical roots and tag-local settings plus schema snapshots now pass, including relative schema files elsewhere inside the repository, historical unknown fields, malformed settings/schema negative controls, path-escape refusals, and default legacy settings. The complete coverage run passed all 475 tests with lines, branches, and functions each exactly 100 percent; public SDK parsing and strict byte/identity validation remain enabled. The separate docstring gate passed. A read-only full-history generation against the pm-cli consumer also passed."
  "2026-09-10T09:20:31.284Z",codex,"Terminal review-fix evidence: npm run release:check passed all 475 tests and exact 100 percent lines/branches/functions, docstrings, production audit, package validation, generated changelog, date guard and publish-attestation guard. The two initial regression failures are preserved as TDD evidence. The real consumer generation also succeeds against the complete pm-cli history."
